('wikiloc', '199743840', 'https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/la-fuente-de-la-carrasca-el-cagasero-piedra-de-la-lobera-las-cabras-la-atalaya-pico-calderon-199743840', 'La Fuente de la Carrasca: El Cagasero - Piedra de La Lobera - Las Cabras - La Atalaya - Pico Calderón', '{"en":"Long loop via Fuente de la Carrasca","ca":"Circular llarga per Fuente de la Carrasca","es":"Circular larga por Fuente de la Carrasca"}'::jsonb, 'La Fuente de la Carrasca: El Cagasero - Piedra de La Lobera - Las Cabras - La Atalaya - Pico Calderón Hiking trail in Cañadas, Castilla-La Mancha (España). Download its GPS track and follow the itinerary on a map. This track leads to the Sierra de Las Cabras, in the province of Albacete. 
This mountain range has the peculiarity of having four peaks close to each other, which are the highest points in the province of Albacete. 
We climbed the peaks of: “El Cagasero” (2,043 m), Piedra de La Lobera (2,018 m), Las Cabras (2,080 m), La Atalaya (2,083 m) the highest point in the province of Albacete, although it is without a triangulation station and Pico Calderón (2071 m), from where we began a beautiful descent through a completely snowy landscape, taking us past “La Piedra de los Enamorados” and the beautiful Sierra de la Taibilla, descending through a lovely reforested pine forest, which coincided with the last stretch of the route. It was the only area from which we could enjoy distant views, in this case of the fields of grain, to the south of the tiny village of Fuente de la Carrasca, which we would reach after passing by the remains of “La Majá de la Percha”, as far as the “distant” mountains of Orce, or “María y Los Veles” some 60 km to the south. 
While we were up in the Sierra, unfortunately we were not able to see anything, no views at all. However, that was due to the bad weather. It was foggy, snowy and the wind was so strong and so cold, that we had to cover our faces with our hands, which were already hurting from the cold. We also stopped taking pictures after a while, wither because our phones had become inactive from the cold or our fingers were too cold already to pull then out of the golves just for taking a photo. 
That tour needs to be repeated in good weather.', '{"en":"This moderate loop route in the Sierra de Las Cabras starts from Fuente de la Carrasca and ascends to five of Albacete''s highest peaks: El Cagasero (2,043 m), Piedra de La Lobera (2,018 m), Las Cabras (2,080 m), La Atalaya (2,083 m), and Pico Calderón (2,071 m).\n\nThe 9.8 km route with 732 m of elevation gain features a descent through a reforested pine forest, passing La Piedra de los Enamorados. While the route offers distant views of grain fields to the south of Fuente de la Carrasca on clear days, conditions can be challenging with fog, snow, and strong winds.","ca":"Aquesta ruta circular moderada a la Sierra de Las Cabras comença a Fuente de la Carrasca i ascendeix a cinc dels cims més alts d''Albacete: El Cagasero (2.043 m), Piedra de La Lobera (2.018 m), Las Cabras (2.080 m), La Atalaya (2.083 m) i Pico Calderón (2.071 m).\n\nEl recorregut de 9,8 km amb 732 m de desnivell positiu inclou un descens per un bosc de pins reforestat, passant per La Piedra de los Enamorados. Tot i que la ruta ofereix vistes llunyanes dels camps de cereals al sud de Fuente de la Carrasca en dies clars, les condicions poden ser difícils amb boira, neu i vents forts.","es":"Esta ruta circular moderada en la Sierra de Las Cabras comienza en Fuente de la Carrasca y asciende a cinco de los picos más altos de Albacete: El Cagasero (2.043 m), Piedra de La Lobera (2.018 m), Las Cabras (2.080 m), La Atalaya (2.083 m) y Pico Calderón (2.071 m).\n\nEl recorrido de 9,8 km con 732 m de desnivel positivo incluye un descenso a través de un pinar reforestado, pasando por La Piedra de los Enamorados. Aunque la ruta ofrece vistas lejanas de los campos de cereal al sur de Fuente de la Carrasca en días despejados, las condiciones pueden ser desafiantes con niebla, nieve y vientos fuertes."}'::jsonb, 'Cut_the_crap', 9769, 732, 732, 2082, 1513, 'moderate', 'loop', 12000, 22500, 1786, '2025-01-29', '2024-12', '[{"lat":38.047811,"lng":-2.404901,"e