- ENGLISH VERSION (https://www.softcatala.org/traductor/). 
 
 
START OF THE WALK. 
We will start the route by leaving the car in a salient of the path that leads to the Hotel Can boix from Peramola, when we reach the restaurant we pass by the side of the barrier, we cross straight the enclosure and continue straight on the path following the Torrent de Rombau, shortly after it becomes a path to which we continue, we go up and follow the signs always towards Sant Honorat. We pass through different points of interest, such as an Oven of Lime and the Balma of Can Boix, reached the Coll de Sant honorat, a monolith in the tribute to Josep Maria Viladrich Bortoló ''Manix'', "a person who has always loved the mountain, the municipality and the valley" and who has worked to spread mountaineering in Oliana and its surroundings. 
 
We continue straight, we pass through interesting details built from past times in the actions on the path to finish climbing to the Sierra de Sant Honorat. 
The Sierra de Sant Honorat is a mountain located in the municipality of Peramola in the Alt Urgell region, with an elevation of 1,066 meters. 
This summit is included in the list of the 100 summits of the FEEC with the name of Saint Honorat 
 
Arriving, close by you can see the remains of the hermitage of Sant Honorat. 
The building has a rectangular floor plan, with no differentiated head, practically demolished, the most unique element is the entrance door, with an arch of sandstone lintel. On the north wall there is an opening. The finding of a capital suggests the possibility of an earlier temple. 
 
From above the plane we go more to the right, to dwarf to one come out of the magnificent cliffs that can reach 300 meters high, where we can see a well of water excavated in the rock and detail of steps next to the well, there are all in the plateau you can admire some wonderful panoramic views of the environment (I recommend the perimeter vault to the plateau on the path). 
 
 We return along the same path approximately 1 km to continue to the right at the intersection, we travel south of Sant Honorat passing, extreme caution is necessary in the passage through the rock, in the last section there is a chain to help if necessary, we will pass through the magnificent rock formations of the Barranc de Sant Honorat until we reach Coll de Mur below the Long Rock. NOTE: The deposits of materials left by the rivers after the formation of the Pyrenean mountain range, at the end of the Tertiary, and the subsequent withdrawal of the sea that occupied the Oliana plain, together with the erosion processes, have left this beautiful rocky ensemble. 
 
We continue towards the Roca del Corb (today we will not go up to the highest point), we will go up to the rock formation of the hermitage of Sant Salvador del Corb and its magnificent panoramic views. The uniqueness of this chapel is caused by its location: it is encinglerated on a small collet between the second and third needle of the Agulles del Corb ensemble. The building is dated to the end of the 11th century. It is considered the smallest Romanesque church in Catalonia (currently this title has a hermitage of Solsonès). 
 
We continue south and soon we turn right again about 400 meters to go to the Cova Casa del Corb. It is a cave about 20 meters deep by about 25 meters wide closed on one side by a wall of wall, which is the oldest part, made on two or three rows of stone, the other part, about 5 meters long, is a wall plastered. The bread oven made of stone stands out. It has indications of having been occupied since prehistory, was inhabited until the 1920s. 
 
The walk continues through the Corb hole. It is a medium-sized tectonic cavity, with small parietal casings at the top. The first known news is that of a partial incursion, towards the end of the 1960s, by a group of young people from Peramola. The first total exploration took place on November 22, 1970. 
 
We continue towards Coll de Quatre Camins, we go to the left, we pass by Grau de Porta and again to the left going down until we reach Can Boix and in the parking of the starting and arrival point of the route. 
 
END OF A MAGNIFICENT WALK!!! 
 
 
